DEP,deposition,Deposition,Conformal HAR film growth at production-worthy throughput,Scientific plus production bottleneck,"Official sources openly recognize the tradeoff between ALD-like conformality and throughput, and the need for batch/vertical solutions.",ALD/LPCVD product mix; validation and repeat-order disclosures; film-process job ads.,Repeat orders are a helpful signal but do not reveal full chamber-match difficulty.,NAURA ALD/LPCVD pages and article; AMEC annual reports; CNINFO
DEP,deposition,Deposition,Coupling precursor chemistry to stable chamber behavior and low particles,Scale-up bottleneck,Lab film quality is easier than stable HVM performance across PM cycles and chamber populations.,In-situ clean messaging; chamber-match language; maintenance and application roles; patents on gas delivery and chamber materials.,Public filings may under-describe maintenance sensitivity and excursion modes.,NAURA and AMEC product pages and annual reports; CNIPA; company ATS
MI,metrology_inspection,Metrology/Inspection,Optics-plus-algorithms integration that reduces false alarms without losing sensitivity,Cross-disciplinary bottleneck,"Inspection and metrology tools publicly emphasize illumination, classification, AI/ML, and yield-ramp support, implying a hard hardware-software boundary problem.","Optical-design and algorithm hiring; product language on ADC, AI, classification, and yield excursion control.",Private datasets and customer libraries mean papers and patents undercount operational skill.,KLA official pages; Skyverse and SMEE product pages; recruitment pages
MI,metrology_inspection,Metrology/Inspection,Field calibration and fab-specific tuning,Service and application bottleneck,"Measurement trust in production depends on calibration, matching, nuisance suppression, and tool-to-tool consistency at customer sites.",Field support roles; annual reports on support teams; service-page language; training plans.,The best know-how is often buried in service routines rather than formal R&D outputs.,Skyverse annual reports and ATS; SMEE service pages; CNINFO
LIT,lithography_sidebar,Lithography Sidebar,"Opto-mechatronic integration for overlay, focus, and stability",System-engineering bottleneck,"ASML’s public decomposition of lithography and SMEE’s published skill requirements both point to a rare combination of optics, mechanics, control, and calibration.",Optical-design job requirements; lithography product pages stressing focus/overlay/backside alignment.,"This row is a sidebar inference for atlas design, not a claim about exact labor shortage magnitude.",ASML lithography pages; SMEE product and recruitment pages; CNIPA
